      "overall_rating": 0,
      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "I chose Solahart because they seemed to have good reviews and recommendations. I thought the Solahart hot water system would go well with the 10 kW solar system as my property does not have room for a heat pump hot water tank.I had talked with the salesman about my long term plan to get an EV and 2 way charger for V2H and I assumed the system he sold me would work for that.I have had several issues with this company and their products and installation:-1 poor communication with keeping me informed about when and who. I thought the salesperson would be my contact through the installation process but there was confusing email messages and no handover nor clear advice about dates.2  I find out 5 months after installation that the Goodwe inverter installed is not compatible with a battery at all.3 I paid for a consumption monitor but they forgot about it during installation and took 3 months to get one and put it in.4 the routing for the hot water is too long and done the easiest way not the best way. It takes a full 2 minutes and 20 litres of water to get hot water at the kitchen tap.5 the Solahart hot water system I was told by the salesman would only require minimal electric boost and only in winter. The consumption meter tells me that it uses up to 8kWh a day on cloudy days even in spring and still uses some electric boost on sunny days. It seems that it needed to be installed with a more optimal northerly aspect.Although the company has begun discussing these issues with me, I cannot recommend this company.",
